"path":232,"stem":233,"icon":234},"CRI Format","\u002Fplatform\u002Freference\u002Fcri-format","04.platform\u002F12.reference\u002F01.cri-format","i-lucide-link",{"title":236,"path":237,"stem":238,"icon":239},"Grind Jobs","\u002Fplatform\u002Freference\u002Fgrind-jobs","04.platform\u002F12.reference\u002F02.grind-jobs","i-lucide-workflow",{"title":241,"path":242,"stem":243,"icon":178},"Project Publishing Design","\u002Fplatform\u002Freference\u002Fproject-publishing-design","04.platform\u002F12.reference\u002F03.project-publishing-design",{"title":245,"path":246,"stem":247,"icon":33},"Sign-In Design","\u002Fplatform\u002Freference\u002Fsign-in-design","04.platform\u002F12.reference\u002F04.sign-in-design",{"title":249,"path":250,"stem":251,"icon":252},"Development Server","\u002Fplatform\u002Fdevelopment-server","04.platform\u002F13.development-server","i-lucide-server-cog",{"title":254,"path":255,"stem":256,"icon":257},"Supply Chain Security","\u002Fplatform\u002Fsupply-chain-security","04.platform\u002F14.supply-chain-security","i-lucide-package-check",{"title":259,"path":260,"stem":261,"icon":262},"Enterprise License","\u002Fplatform\u002Fenterprise-license","04.platform\u002F15.enterprise-license","i-lucide-badge-check",{"id":264,"title":254,"body":265,"description":778,"extension":779,"links":780,"meta":781,"navigation":782,"path":255,"seo":783,"stem":256,"__hash__":784},"docs\u002F04.platform\u002F14.supply-chain-security.md",{"type":266,"value":267,"toc":762},"minimark",[268,272,285,290,350,354,358,460,464,524,528,588,592,627,631,677,681],[269,270,26],"h2",{"id":271},"overview",[273,274,275,276,280,281,284],"p",{},"Every Kinotic service image is inventoried and scanned for known vulnerabilities before it is published. An image with a Critical vulnerability that has a published fix is never promoted to Docker Hub. Every control on this page runs automatically in the ",[277,278,279],"code",{},"Build and Publish"," workflow (",[277,282,283],{},".github\u002Fworkflows\u002Fgradle-build.yml","), and each one leaves evidence in GitHub.",[286,287,289],"h3",{"id":288},"scope","Scope",[291,292,293,306],"table",{},[294,295,296],"thead",{},[297,298,299,303],"tr",{},[300,301,302],"th",{},"Image",[300,304,305],{},"Published as",[307,308,309,320,330,340],"tbody",{},[297,310,311,315],{},[312,313,314],"td",{},"Kinotic management server",[312,316,317],{},[277,318,319],{},"kinoticai\u002Fkinotic-server-management",[297,321,322,325],{},[312,323,324],{},"Kinotic system server",[312,326,327],{},[277,328,329],{},"kinoticai\u002Fkinotic-server-system",[297,331,332,335],{},[312,333,334],{},"Kinotic app server",[312,336,337],{},[277,338,339],{},"kinoticai\u002Fkinotic-server-app",[297,341,342,345],{},[312,343,344],{},"Kinotic migration",[312,346,347],{},[277,348,349],{},"kinoticai\u002Fkinotic-migration",[269,351,353],{"id":352},"controls","Controls",[286,355,357],{"id":356},"software-inventory-sbom","Software inventory (SBOM)",[291,359,360,368],{},[294,361,362],{},[297,363,364,366],{},[300,365],{},[300,367],{},[307,369,370,381,399,417,450],{},[297,371,372,378],{},[312,373,374],{},[375,376,377],"strong",{},"Control",[312,379,380],{},"Each build produces a software bill of materials for each image, one for its amd64 build and one for its arm64 build, the two platforms its published tag holds. It lists every operating-system package and application library in the image, with its version.",[297,382,383,388],{},[312,384,385],{},[375,386,387],{},"Format",[312,389,390,391,398],{},"CycloneDX JSON, generated with ",[392,393,397],"a",{"href":394,"rel":395},"https:\u002F\u002Fgithub.com\u002Fanchore\u002Fsyft",[396],"nofollow","Syft"," from the built image, not from source manifests. The inventory therefore matches what runs.",[297,400,401,406],{},[312,402,403],{},[375,404,405],{},"Frequency",[312,407,408,409,412,413,416],{},"Every build of the images: each pull request into ",[277,410,411],{},"develop"," or ",[277,414,415],{},"main",", each push to them that changes application code, and nightly.",[297,418,419,424],{},[312,420,421],{},[375,422,423],{},"Evidence",[312,425,426,427,430,431,430,434,437,438,441,442,445,446,449],{},"Workflow run artifacts named ",[277,428,429],{},"sbom-kinotic-server-management.cdx.json",", ",[277,432,433],{},"sbom-kinotic-server-system.cdx.json",[277,435,436],{},"sbom-kinotic-server-app.cdx.json"," and ",[277,439,440],{},"sbom-kinotic-migration.cdx.json"," for the amd64 builds, and the same names with ",[277,443,444],{},"-arm64"," before ",[277,447,448],{},".cdx.json"," for the arm64 builds.",[297,451,452,457],{},[312,453,454],{},[375,455,456],{},"Retention",[312,458,459],{},"90 days.",[286,461,463],{"id":462},"vulnerability-scanning","Vulnerability scanning",[291,465,466,474],{},[294,467,468],{},[297,469,470,472],{},[300,471],{},[300,473],{},[307,475,476,490,499],{},[297,477,478,482],{},[312,479,480],{},[375,481,377],{},[312,483,484,489],{},[392,485,488],{"href":486,"rel":487},"https:\u002F\u002Fgithub.com\u002Fanchore\u002Fgrype",[396],"Grype"," scans each image's SBOM against current vulnerability advisories: GitHub Security Advisories, the National Vulnerability Database, and operating-system vendor feeds. The scan covers the same artifact the inventory records.",[297,491,492,496],{},[312,493,494],{},[375,495,405],{},[312,497,498],{},"Every build, including each pull request, and nightly. The nightly run checks newly published advisories against the current images.",[297,500,501,505],{},[312,502,503],{},[375,504,423],{},[312,506,507,508,430,511,430,514,437,517,520,521,523],{},"Findings of every severity are recorded as GitHub code scanning alerts in the categories ",[277,509,510],{},"image-kinotic-server-management",[277,512,513],{},"image-kinotic-server-system",[277,515,516],{},"image-kinotic-server-app",[277,518,519],{},"image-kinotic-migration"," for the amd64 builds, and the same categories with ",[277,522,444],{}," appended for the arm64 builds, with open and fixed history per finding. Each workflow run's summary lists the fixable findings for each image and platform.",[286,525,527],{"id":526},"release-gate","Release gate",[291,529,530,538],{},[294,531,532],{},[297,533,534,536],{},[300,535],{},[300,537],{},[307,539,540,558,568],{},[297,541,542,546],{},[312,543,544],{},[375,545,377],{},[312,547,548,549,552,553,412,555,557],{},"A build fails when either image has a ",[375,550,551],{},"Critical"," vulnerability with a published fix. On a pull request, the failure is reported on the change before it merges. Only an image from a fully passing build of ",[277,554,411],{},[277,556,415],{}," is promoted from the staging registry (ghcr.io) to Docker Hub.",[297,559,560,565],{},[312,561,562],{},[375,563,564],{},"Effect",[312,566,567],{},"An image is published only when, at build time, it has no known Critical vulnerability with an available fix.",[297,569,570,574],{},[312,571,572],{},[375,573,423],{},[312,575,576,577,580,581,584,585,587],{},"The ",[277,578,579],{},"SBOM and Vulnerability Scan"," jobs and the ",[277,582,583],{},"Build Result"," job of each workflow run. ",[277,586,583],{}," performs the promotion and records which job withheld it.",[286,589,591],{"id":590},"integrity-of-the-scanning-tools","Integrity of the scanning tools",[291,593,594,602],{},[294,595,596],{},[297,597,598,600],{},[300,599],{},[300,601],{},[307,603,604,613],{},[297,605,606,610],{},[312,607,608],{},[375,609,377],{},[312,611,612],{},"Third-party actions in the scan job are pinned to full commit SHAs rather than version tags, so a repointed tag cannot change the code that runs. The scan job has read-only access to repository contents and holds no publishing, signing or deployment credentials.",[297,614,615,620],{},[312,616,617],{},[375,618,619],{},"Maintenance",[312,621,622,623,626],{},"Dependabot proposes updates to every workflow action weekly, including the pinned SHAs (",[277,624,625],{},".github\u002Fdependabot.yml",").",[286,628,630],{"id":629},"source-code-analysis","Source code analysis",[291,632,633,641],{},[294,634,635],{},[297,636,637,639],{},[300,638],{},[300,640],{},[307,642,643,652,664],{},[297,644,645,649],{},[312,646,647],{},[375,648,377],{},[312,650,651],{},"CodeQL static analysis of the Java and TypeScript source.",[297,653,654,658],{},[312,655,656],{},[375,657,405],{},[312,659,660,661,663],{},"Every push to ",[277,662,411],{},", and weekly.",[297,665,666,670],{},[312,667,668],{},[375,669,423],{},[312,671,672,673,676],{},"GitHub code scanning alerts from the ",[277,674,675],{},"CodeQL"," workflow.",[269,678,680],{"id":679},"control-mapping","Control mapping",[291,682,683,698],{},[294,684,685],{},[297,686,687,689,692,695],{},[300,688,377],{},[300,690,691],{},"NIST SP 800-171 Rev 2",[300,693,694],{},"SOC 2",[300,696,697],{},"ISO\u002FIEC 27001:2022",[307,699,700,713,725,738,751],{},[297,701,702,704,707,710],{},[312,703,357],{},[312,705,706],{},"3.4.1",[312,708,709],{},"CC7.1",[312,711,712],{},"A.5.9, A.8.9",[297,714,715,717,720,722],{},[312,716,463],{},[312,718,719],{},"3.11.2",[312,721,709],{},[312,723,724],{},"A.8.8",[297,726,727,729,732,735],{},[312,728,527],{},[312,730,731],{},"3.11.3, 3.14.1",[312,733,734],{},"CC7.1, CC8.1",[312,736,737],{},"A.8.8, A.8.32",[297,739,740,742,745,748],{},[312,741,591],{},[312,743,744],{},"3.4.1, 3.14.1",[312,746,747],{},"CC8.1",[312,749,750],{},"A.8.25, A.8.28",[297,752,753,755,757,759],{},[312,754,630],{},[312,756,719],{},[312,758,709],{},[312,760,761],{},"A.8.28",{"title":763,"searchDepth":764,"depth":764,"links":765},"",2,[766,770,777],{"id":271,"depth":764,"text":26,"children":767},[768],{"id":288,"depth":769,"text":289},3,{"id":352,"depth":764,"text":353,"children":771},[772,773,774,775,776],{"id":356,"depth":769,"text":357},{"id":462,"depth":769,"text":463},{"id":526,"depth":769,"text":527},{"id":590,"depth":769,"text":591},{"id":629,"depth":769,"text":630},{"id":679,"depth":764,"text":680},"How Kinotic inventories, scans and gates the container images it publishes, and where the evidence for each control is kept.","md",null,{},{"icon":257},{"title":254,"description":778},"3bxL12YLlGxJ2XhWn3LghQJw0kqDVah8TbqiylwY34M",[786,788],{"title":249,"path":250,"stem":251,"description":787,"icon":252,"children":-1},"A development environment for a few peers on one physical host, what it keeps in Azure, and how their applications move to Kinotic Cloud.",{"title":259,"path":260,"stem":261,"description":789,"icon":262,"children":-1},"Which parts of Kinotic are Enterprise Features, what running them in production requires, and how the license treats substitute implementations.",1794218632345]